    "https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/9GKM7/Dean-Faculty-of-Agriculture-Life-Sciences,2026-25646.html": {
      "title": "Dean, Faculty of Agriculture & Life Sciences",
      "description": "Dean, Faculty of Agriculture & Life Sciences -\n        Lincoln University Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search careers@lincoln.ac.nz Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Dean, Faculty of Agriculture & Life Sciences Set the direction for one of Australasia's leading land-based institutions. The opportunity Te Whare Wānaka o Aoraki Lincoln University is New Zealand’s specialist land-based university. We grow the knowledge that helps shape a better relationship between land, food and ecosystems. The Faculty of Agriculture and Life Sciences (AGLS) is core to that purpose. As the University’s most research-intensive faculty, it is home to internationally recognised expertise in production systems, conservation and life sciences. As Dean, you will lead a community of researchers and academics working to address challenges and opportunities facing New Zealand’s land-based sectors. This is an appointment for a leader who wants to build. Lincoln University is one of the most postgraduate-intensive universities in Australasia and is developing a new ten-year strategy to be launched ahead of our 150th anniversary in 2028. The incoming Dean will play a pivotal role shaping the Faculty’s future. Why this role, and why now A genuine platform to lead. There is exciting work ahead in refreshing the curriculum, strengthening the academic portfolio and growing the Faculty’s international engagement. You will set the vision and chart the course. Foundation for what's next. Deanships at Lincoln provide a foundation for senior university leadership, and the successful candidate will join an extended leadership team helping steer the University’s next chapter. International reach. Lincoln University is a longstanding partner in the EuroLeague for Life Sciences (ELLS) and has international relationships and momentum an incoming Dean can build on immediately. A place people choose to stay. Canterbury offers an exceptional quality of life. The outdoors, strong schools, and a welcoming community within easy reach of Christchurch. What you’ll lead Reporting to the Provost, you will hold overall accountability for the Faculty’s strategic direction, academic performance, financial sustainability and people. You will: Set and deliver a Faculty strategy that advances excellence in research, education and stakeholder impact. Lead curriculum renewal and portfolio development, ensuring academic offerings remain relevant, industry-connected, and financially sustainable. Sustain and grow research impact, diversifying research income through industry, international and alternative funding, and positioning the Faculty to lead major collaborative research programmes. Build productive partnerships across industry, government, community, iwi and international collaborators, and act as a visible ambassador for the Faculty and University. Strengthen research, education and engagement partnerships with iwi and hapū, advancing the University’s commitments under Te Tiriti o Waitangi. What you’ll bring Strong academic credentials with a land-based orientation. A PhD is preferred. A recognised track record of research leadership and success in building strategic research partnerships. Demonstrated success leading curriculum renewal, portfolio development and programme innovation. Experience leading complex organisational, academic and cultural change with sound financial and workforce judgement. A transparent, energetic leadership style with the credibility to advocate for the Faculty within the University and beyond. A genuine appreciation of what it means to be a small and specialist university, and a commitment to Manaakitaka and Lincoln University’s values. How to apply Lincoln University has partnered with Sheffield Search for this important appointment. To apply in strict confidence now, visit: https://www.sheffield.co.nz/Job-Search?Id=735 or email your cover letter and CV in a PDF format wherever possible to cvwlg@sheffield.co.nz quoting 9088. Applications close on 5 October at 9.00am. Emails will be electronically acknowledged and further correspondence may be by email. For more information please phone Patrick Rooney on +64 21 458 362. Job Details Reference # 2026-25646 Posted on 16 Sep 2026 Closes on 05 Oct 2026 09:00 NZST Location(s) Lincoln University Campus Expertise Academic, General Mgmt/Executive Work type(s) Permanent full-time More details (document) Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Back © Lincoln University Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 10 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance. Loading . . ."
    },
    "https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/wDKM7/Dean-Faculty-of-Agribusiness-Commerce,2026-25645.html": {
      "title": "Dean, Faculty of Agribusiness & Commerce",
      "description": "Dean, Faculty of Agribusiness & Commerce -\n        Lincoln University Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search careers@lincoln.ac.nz Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Dean, Faculty of Agribusiness & Commerce Lead business education and research with its roots in the land, and its reach around the world. The opportunity Te Whare Wānaka o Aoraki Lincoln University is New Zealand’s only specialist university, focused on the land-based sectors, recognised for its contribution to the future of food, fibre, agribusiness, sustainability and the environment. The Faculty of Agribusiness and Commerce is central to the University’s distinctive identity and purpose. Through excellent education and impactful research, the Faculty advances knowledge and leadership across agribusiness, economics, finance, marketing, property, tourism and related disciplines, helping address the opportunities and challenges facing New Zealand’s land-based sectors. This is a rare chance to lead the next stage of growth and ambition for this important Faculty. Why this role, and why now Build on real strength. Agribusiness and Commerce contributes significantly to the University. The opportunity ahead is to deepen its research impact and international footprint while sustaining excellent, industry-connected education. Accreditation on the horizon. Pursuing AACSB accreditation is a strategic priority, and experience of that journey, or the appetite to lead it, will be highly valued. Foundation for what's next. Deanships at Lincoln provide a foundation for senior university leadership, and the successful candidate will join an extended leadership team helping steer the University’s next chapter. An exceptional place to live and lead. Canterbury offers an exceptional quality of life. The outdoors, strong schools, and a welcoming community within easy reach of Christchurch. What you’ll lead Reporting to the Provost, you will hold primary accountability for the Faculty’s strategy, academic performance, financial sustainability and people. You will: Set and deliver a Faculty strategy that advances excellence in teaching, research and stakeholder impact. Lead continuous improvement of the taught portfolio keeping it relevant, rigorous, industry-connected and financially sustainable. Provide leadership for the Faculty’s pursuit and maintenance of AACSB accreditation and other quality frameworks. Grow a strong culture of research excellence, lifting external research income, high-quality publications and a growth in postgraduate enrolments. Develop international partnerships that support education, research and student opportunities. Act as a visible ambassador across industry, government, community, iwi and professional networks. Strengthen research, education and engagement partnerships with iwi and hapū, advancing the University’s commitments under Te Tiriti o Waitangi. What you’ll bring A PhD or equivalent professional experience is required, ideally with a land-based, agribusiness, business or commerce orientation. Demonstrated ability to lead and foster a culture of research excellence, innovation and impact, with an understanding of the drivers of research performance and income. Success in curriculum renewal, programme development and academic quality enhancement. Experience leading complex organisational, cultural and operational change in higher education or comparable environments. The ability to build strong relationships with industry, government, international and iwi partners. A transparent, energetic and empathetic leadership style, and a genuine appreciation of what it means to be a small and specialist university, and a commitment to Manaakitaka and Lincoln University’s values. How to apply Lincoln University has partnered with Sheffield Search for this important appointment. To apply in strict confidence now, visit: https://www.sheffield.co.nz/Job-Search?Id=736 or email your cover letter and CV in a PDF format wherever possible to cvwlg@sheffield.co.nz quoting 9087. Applications close on 5 October at 9.00am. Emails will be electronically acknowledged and further correspondence may be by email. For more information please phone Patrick Rooney on +64 21 458 362. Job Details Reference # 2026-25645 Posted on 16 Sep 2026 Closes on 05 Oct 2026 09:00 NZST Location(s) Lincoln University Campus Expertise Academic, General Mgmt/Executive Work type(s) Permanent full-time More details (document) Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Back © Lincoln University Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 10 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance. Loading . . ."
    },
    "https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/N4CM7/Multimedia-Content-Creator,2026-25536.html": {
      "title": "Multimedia Content Creator",
      "description": "Multimedia Content Creator -\n        Lincoln University Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search careers@lincoln.ac.nz Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Multimedia Content Creator Create engaging multimedia content that enhances learning, teaching and research through video, photography, podcasts, graphics and animation. Mō te tūka | The role As our Multimedia Content Creator, you'll help bring learning, teaching and research to life through high-quality digital media. Based in our Learning, Teaching and Library team, you'll work closely with academic staff, the Video and Multimedia Specialist, and other University stakeholders to create engaging multimedia content that supports an outstanding student experience. Some tasks of the role include: Creating and producing videos, photography, podcasts, graphics and animations Supporting multimedia productions both on campus and off site, including filming, editing and quality control Coordinating production schedules and supporting multiple multimedia projects Maintaining organised multimedia records and content management systems Staying up to date with emerging digital media technologies and best practice Promoting and supporting the effective use of multimedia in education This is a creative and collaborative role where you'll be involved in the full production process, from planning and filming through to editing and final delivery. You'll have the opportunity to work across a variety of projects, helping to showcase innovative teaching practices and research outcomes through modern digital media. Mahi & Wāhi / Utu | Work pattern, location & salary This permanent role is based at our Lincoln Campus and works 37.5 hours per week (1.0 FTE). The salary range for this position is $62,000 - $67,000 per annum, depending on experience. Kā tino Pūkeka/Whēako | Essential skills/experience for the role To be successful in the role you will have A relevant tertiary qualification and at least one year of experience in multimedia content creation or a related field Experience creating and editing original video and multimedia content across a variety of formats Strong skills in video production, filming, editing and the use of production equipment such as cameras and lighting Experience using industry-standard software such as Adobe Creative Suite (including Photoshop, Premiere Pro and After Effects) and/or Final Cut Pro Excellent organisational, problem-solving and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work collaboratively as part of a team The ability to communicate technical concepts clearly to non-technical audiences and provide outstanding client service A passion for creativity, innovation and continuous learning, along with a commitment to Lincoln University's values and collaborative culture, will set you up for success in this role. Kā hua ka riro ki a koe | What's in it for you? Join a supportive, inclusive community that values diversity, wellbeing, and professional growth. Benefits include: Flexible, family‑friendly work + free on‑site parking Professional development & mentorship to grow your career Generous leave entitlements – six weeks of paid leave per year (based on 1.0 FTE) Annual salary reviews to recognise your contribution Contributions toward eye tests and prescription eyewear Free, confidential wellbeing support through Clearhead (EAP) Southern Cross employee benefits Access to on‑campus gym with discounted membership On‑site early childhood centre with staff discounts A vibrant campus lifestyle with cafés, green spaces, and a sense of community Mō mātou | About us Te Whare Wānaka o Aoraki | Lincoln University is a specialist institution dedicated to impactful research and higher education that supports land-based industries in New Zealand and globally. Our campus sits at the heart of the Lincoln research precinct, complemented by university-owned farms and research stations that blend education, research, and hands-on learning. At Lincoln, students are at the heart of everything we do, empower them to grow their potential and contribute to a more sustainably productive world through world-class teaching and research. As a progressive university with an ambitious vision, we value a professional workforce that reflects the diversity of our community. Our staff engage with students, parents, government, iwi, and external stakeholders, upholding Lincoln University’s reputation through their work. Our Te Tiriti o Waitangi commitments begin with mana whenua. We honour our special relationship with Ngāi Te Ruahikihiki and Te Taumutu Rūnanga, embedded in our He Tūtohinga Whakamātau | Charter of Understanding. Tono ināianei | Apply now Ready to apply? Submit your CV and a cover letter that highlights your fit - tell us why you want this role and what motivates you to join Lincoln University. Applications received via email will not be considered, however specific enquiry relating to the role can be made to Tracy-Anne.DeSilva@lincoln.ac.nz We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community where everyone feels valued and supported, and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. We are only considering applicants who have current unrestricted legal working rights in New Zealand. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this role. View the position description at: https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz Job Details Reference # 2026-25536 Posted on 16 Sep 2026 Closes on 04 Oct 2026 18:00 NZST Location(s) Lincoln University Campus Expertise Administration, Communications Work type(s) Permanent full-time More details (document) PD Multimedia Content Creator September 2026.pdf Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Back © Lincoln University Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 10 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance. Loading . . ."
    }
  },
